/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (SST \(Speech-to-Text\) is a technology that converts human speech or voice commands into written text. For example, when a user says, "Turn on the lights," the SST system processes the user's voice and converts it into the text "Turn on the lights." The system can then analyze this text and perform the requested action.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
